# Paper running example (Asma et al., NPCS, WWW'24 — Example 3.2), encoded with
# SPARQL-star / RDF-star: a quoted triple << s p o >> is linked to its provenance
# token u_i via ex:occurrenceOf (the predicate NPCS's SPARQL_Star scheme matches).
# The same quoted triple with two occurrenceOf tokens (u1, u2) yields (u1 ⊕ u2).
#
# Use with:  java -cp target/npcs-rewrite.jar npcs.RunExample SPARQL_Star \
#              examples/data/example.star.ttls <query.sparql>

@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/paper#> .
@prefix occ: <http://example.org/> .          # occ:occurrenceOf is the predicate NPCS's SPARQL_Star scheme matches

# --- Example 3.2 (verbatim): Alice ---
<< ex:Alice ex:likes   ex:pasta >> occ:occurrenceOf ex:u1 .
<< ex:Alice ex:likes   ex:pasta >> occ:occurrenceOf ex:u2 .
<< ex:Alice ex:livesIn ex:Italy >> occ:occurrenceOf ex:u3 .

# --- Added so UNION / MINUS / OPTIONAL return non-trivial provenance ---
<< ex:Bob   ex:likes   ex:pasta >> occ:occurrenceOf ex:u4 .
<< ex:Carol ex:livesIn ex:Italy >> occ:occurrenceOf ex:u5 .
